.TH MD_GET_GEOMETRY 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_geometry \- query the actual FFT and timing geometry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_get_geometry(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, struct
    morsedec_geometry *geometry);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query the actual FFT and timing geometry.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I geometry
Non-NULL output structure; receives a caller-owned copy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
decoder or geometry is NULL.
.SH REMARKS
Returns the effective sample_rate, fft_size, hop_size, spectrum_size,
first_frequency, bin_spacing and frame_seconds. Automatic sizes and band edges
are rounded; query this structure instead of assuming the requested edges were
exact. Spectrum bin j has frequency first_frequency+j*bin_spacing. For I/Q,
this is a signed Hz offset. frame_seconds=hop_size/sample_rate and
bin_spacing=sample_rate/fft_size. The configuration is immutable, so these
values remain valid across reset and flush.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_new (3),
.BR md_new_iq (3),
.BR md_process_spectrum (3)
